To determine a number on each vertex of the equilateral triangle we use the following rules:

• The number over a side of the triangle is added to both vertices that make up that side.

• When the number over a side of the triangle is positive, it is added to the value of the vertices. When the number over a side of the triangle is negative, it is subtracted from the value of the vertices.

Let’s now describe how the final values at the vertices are calculated for the triangle below:

